    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d314">

                <pb facs="0445" n="365" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg365"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Brun</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-10-18"><hi rendition="#italic">October 18,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Brun</hi>: In reply to your inquiry the
                    other day, I take pleasure in saying that, if you desire it, I will instruct our
                    minister in San Salvador to use his good offices in behalf of any Danish
                    subjects for whom they are desired, assuming, of course, that the Government of
                    Salvador will make no objection.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
